claim.claim-text:
a first switching element (S2 - Fig. 29);
a second switching element (S3);
an output bump (BB1, BB2);
an interconnect region including a first sub-region extending from the first switching element (S2) to a first node (N2), a second region extending from the second switching element (S3) to the first node (N2), and a third sub-region extending from the first node (N2) to the output bump (BB1, BB2);
wherein the first sub-region comprises:
a first plurality of metallization levels (201 - Figs. 30, 31) interconnected by vias, the first plurality of metallization levels (201) each including a metal sheet (203, 202) extending completely from the first switching element (S2) to the first node (N2) to directly electrically connect the first switching element (S2) to the first node (N2);
a second plurality of metallization levels (204a) interconnected by vias, the second plurality of metallization levels (204a) overlying the first plurality of metallization levels (201) and interconnected thereto by vias, the second plurality of metallization levels (204a) each including a metal sheet (207a, 206a, 205a) extending from the first switching element (S2) partially toward the first node (N2);

wherein the second sub-region comprises:
a first plurality of metallization levels (201) interconnected by vias, the first plurality of metallization levels (201) of the second sub-region each including a metal sheet (203, 202) extending completely from the second switching element (S3) to the first node (N2) to directly electrically connect the second switching element (S3) to the first node (N2);
a second plurality of metallization levels (204b) interconnected by vias, the second plurality of metallization levels (204b) of the second sub-region overlying the first plurality of metallization levels (201) of the second sub-region and interconnected thereto by vias, the second plurality of metallization levels (204b) of the second sub-region each including a metal sheet (207b, 206b, 205b) extending from the second switching element (S3) partially toward the first node (N2), defining a break (210) between the second plurality of metallization levels (204b) of the second sub-region and the second plurality of metallization levels (204a) of the first sub-region;

a first plurality of metallization levels (203, 202) interconnected by vias and extending from the first node (N2) to the output bump (BB1. BB2) to directly electrically connect the first node (N2) to the output bump (BB1, BB2); and
a second plurality of metallization levels (207c, 206c, 205c) interconnected by vias, the second plurality of metallization levels (207c, 206c, 205c) of the third sub-region overlying the first plurality of metallization levels (203, 202) of the third sub-region and interconnected thereto by vias;
wherein the second plurality of metallization levels (207c, 206c, 205c) of the third sub-region include:

a first underlying metallization level (206c) overlying the first plurality of metallization levels (203, 202) of the third sub-region and interconnected thereto by vias, the first underlying metallization level (206c) including a plurality of spaced apart metal sheets connected to the first plurality of metallization levels (203, 202) of the third sub-region by the vias; and
a second underlying metallization level (205c) overlying the first underlying metallization level (206c) and interconnected thereto by vias, the second underlying metallization level (205c) including a plurality of spaced apart metal sheets connecting the spaced apart metal sheets of the first underlying metallization level (206c) to the metal sheet of the top metallization level (207c);
wherein the plurality of spaced apart metal sheets of the first underlying metallization level (206c) and corresponding ones of the plurality of spaced apart metal sheets of the second underlying metallization level (205c) are connected by the vias to define a plurality of spaced apart conductive pillars that are connected in parallel between the top metallization level (207c) and the first underlying metallization level (206c).
